# Cloudflare Pages edge response headers
# (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/)
#
# Goal: prevent runtime-config files from being cached as `immutable` by
# CDN/browser. SvelteKit's `adapter-static` writes two files at the
# `_app/` root whose contents change per-deploy (they don't carry a
# content-hash in their filename):
#
#   * `_app/env.js`         — `export const env = {...}` from
#                              `$env/dynamic/public`. Holds runtime URLs
#                              (PUBLIC_PROOF_STORE_URL, PUBLIC_AUTH_API_URL,
#                              etc). If this ships with `Cache-Control:
#                              immutable, max-age=31536000` then a browser
#                              that ever loaded an EMPTY `env={}` (e.g.
#                              from a CI build that ran without `.env`)
#                              never re-fetches it — SDK silently takes
#                              the no-proofs path, `claimableNow` stays
#                              `null`, UI shows `0.000000 RWT`.
#   * `_app/version.json`   — `{"version":"<timestamp>"}` used by the
#                              client runtime to detect new deploys and
#                              auto-reload. Same problem if cached
#                              immutable.
#
# Everything under `_app/immutable/` IS content-hashed (e.g.
# `app.D5z2Glgd.js`) and is safe to cache forever — those filenames
# change on every meaningful content change, so the long max-age is the
# point. Keep that rule too, in case the upstream CDN config drifts.

/_app/env.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/_app/version.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/_app/immutable/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
